bigrams.json — letter-bigram table of the need-OCR classifier

- Content: log10 P(b|a) letter-bigram tables, add-one smoothing, "ё" folded into "е", 3 decimals.
- "ru" (32 letters): counted from public-domain Russian texts of ru.wikisource.org (plain page
  text, about 1.12 M letter pairs, half literature and half law; a fixed letter-pair budget per
  work, long works cut at a prefix):
  - literature, PD-old-70: Тургенев «Отцы и дети»; Достоевский «Бедные люди»; Лермонтов «Герой
    нашего времени»; Пушкин «Капитанская дочка»; Чехов «Остров Сахалин»; Куприн «Поединок»
    (I–VI, IX); Ключевский «Курс русской истории» (лекции I–II);
  - law, PD-RU-exempt (official documents, Civil Code of the RF art. 1259(6)): Конституция
    Российской Федерации; Уголовный кодекс РФ; Трудовой кодекс РФ; Гражданский кодекс РФ
    (the main page and chapters of each).
- "en" (26 letters): counted from the ground-truth Markdown of opendataloader-bench (Apache-2.0),
  unchanged from the first table. That corpus is taken from the DP-Bench dataset (Upstage,
  MIT licence, https://huggingface.co/datasets/upstage/dp-bench; documents from the Library of
  Congress, open educational resources and the authors' own files, per its card). The table
  holds only letter-pair frequencies (log10 probabilities to 3 decimals), no text of the
  documents; the benchmark repository and the dataset are credited here.
- Built by the research script `build_pd.py RU_DIR EN_DIR OUT.json` (same procedure as the
  ocr-need `scripts/build_bigrams.py`, outside the repository); pinned sha256
  8b20b8d441981919706100317740d02ec7f3f92d1e569caf19d4358b342a170b (`build.rs` and
  `Bigrams::from_bytes` refuse any other file). The golden `bigram_lp` values are computed with
  exactly this file. The classifier thresholds (`bigram` -1.35 / -1.9) were calibrated by the
  research on its Russian Wikipedia table and are kept unchanged: the task 14a gate gives the
  same result with this table.
- No data derived from Wikipedia (CC BY-SA) is included: the "ru" half is counted only from the
  public-domain texts listed above.
- Deleting the file is enough for a build without the table: the classifier then runs without the
  bigram rule (one Info warning per PDF).
